# Architecture Rules for DavidAgent Self-Evolving Agent V2.0

This file contains the distilled architectural rules from OpenSpec v1.0 and MCP protocol.

## Core Principles
- Recursive self-reflection and logical self-healing
- Spontaneous tool creation with MCP compliance  
- Strong physical anchoring with environment feedback
- Architectural constraint awareness with topology mapping
- Memory metabolism and entropy reduction

## Enforcement Rules
1. NO_SDD_NO_CODE: All development requires SDD specification
2. SDD_COMPLIANCE_REQUIRED: SDD must follow OpenSpec v1.0 four pillars
3. GITHUB_SYNC_MANDATORY: Specs must be pushed to GitHub /specs/
4. ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW_REQUIRED: Architecture coach audit mandatory
5. SANDBOX_TESTING_REQUIRED: Shadow sandbox testing before production
6. TOPOLOGY_AWARENESS: Real-time system topology analysis required

## Architecture Coach Authority
- Highest veto power over all architectural decisions
- Independent audit layer for all self-evolution activities
- Real-time monitoring of component dependencies and constraints

